meta {
  name: Declare income (ISA)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/contracts/{{contractId}}/income-declarations
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~asOf: 2027-06-02
}

headers {
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{studentToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "period": "2027-05",
    "grossMonthlyIncomeCents": 215000
  }
}

docs {
  Income share agreements only: the student declares the gross income of a month (`period` as YYYY-MM; 0 when none), from its first day until the end of the 4th of the next month. On the 5th the month is assessed and charged; a closed or assessed month answers `period_not_open`. The happy path contract is an instalment loan, so this answers an error there: sign in as `bruno.silva@example.com`, whose seeded contract is an ISA, or apply with `"product": { "kind": "isa" }`. An ISA signed today starts paying months from now (`firstPeriod` in "Get schedule"): put that month in `period`, enable `asOf` with the 2nd of the month after it (accepted where `BILLING_FUTURE_RUNS_ENABLED` is on, the default outside production), then "Run billing (ops)" as of the 5th of that month to see the share charged and collected.
}
